{
  "note": "C-AUTO-02's committed encoding fixture: 40 bodies with the encoding, unit count, segment count and remaining budget each one must produce, hand authored case by case. The expectations are committed, so a change to the GSM-7 alphabet, to either capacity or to the cluster-safe split fails packages/core/src/messaging/segments.fixture.test.ts rather than changing a price quietly. `units` is septets for GSM-7 and UTF-16 code units for UCS-2; `unitSegments` is ceil(units / perSegment) and differs from `segments` only where keeping a grapheme whole costs a segment the arithmetic does not charge for. Invisible characters are written as \\u escapes so the file can be reviewed; no name of a person appears in any body (ADR 0020).",
  "limits": {
    "GSM-7": {
      "single": 160,
      "concatenated": 153
    },
    "UCS-2": {
      "single": 70,
      "concatenated": 67
    }
  },
